  "body": "Not a lot: orchestrator claim PR (ORCHESTRATION.md, Claims).\n\n- Claims wave 1 for child sessions: LOT-043 (Opus), LOT-024 (Sonnet), LOT-034 (Fable), LOT-023 (Sonnet), LOT-036 (Sonnet), LOT-037 (Sonnet) — owner `mac/w1-<lot>-<model> (2026-10-27)`, `in-progress`. Every dependency of each is `done`; captures and legacy-oracle outputs exist (LOT-002/003/004 fixtures) per LESSONS 35.\n- Adds a **Wave plan** section: MVP definition (LOT-080..083 + engine deps, login/session, posting basics), wave 1 with tracks and author → reviewer models (AGENTS §6), wave 2 planned.\n\nTouches only `docs/LOTS.md`. `check-lot-deps.py` and markdownlint pass locally.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CHteTFWfkJGeSNGpSW\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Updated project planning documentation to show six work items as in progress, with assigned owners and claim dates.\n  * Added a two-wave plan outlining the MVP scope, app track, work assignments, reviewers, and dependencies, making the planned work and its sequencing clearer.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
